    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0594" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg380"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 168.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Mr.
                        Bancroft</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 319.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 17, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received, and perused with much
                    interest, your dispatch of the 22d ultimo, No. 206.</p>
                <p>Your statement in regard to effect produced in Germany by the message of the
                    President to Congress announcing the union of South <pb facs="0595" n="381"
                        xml:id="pg381"/> with North Germany is very gratifying, and your sketch of
                    the organization and policy of united Germany and the progress of liberal
                    political views in the states composing the new German empire, together with
                    your account of the speech of the Emperor at the first sitting of the parliament
                    of Germany, are equally so.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
